## Batch Processing

### Batch Types

| Type | Flow |
|---|---|
| `metadata` | FE calls `createBatch` -> gets pre-signed PUT URLs -> uploads TSVs to S3 -> calls `updateBatch` -> backend sends `Load Metadata` to SQS |
| `data file` | FE/CLI calls `createBatch` -> backend generates DRS IDs -> CLI calls `createTempCredentials` -> CLI uploads to S3 directly -> CLI calls `updateBatch` |

### Batch Statuses

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Uploading` | Batch created, files being uploaded |
| `Uploaded` | All files uploaded successfully |
| `Failed` | One or more files failed to upload |

### Metadata Batch Upload Sequence

```
FE: createBatch(submissionID, "metadata", ["file1.tsv", "file2.tsv"])
  -> BE returns: {batchID, files: [{fileName, signedURL}, ...]}
FE: PUT each file to its signedURL
FE: updateBatch(batchID, [{fileName, succeeded: true}, ...])
  -> BE verifies S3 uploads, sends "Load Metadata" SQS message
  -> External validator service picks up, parses TSVs, writes dataRecords
```

### Data File Batch Upload Sequence

```
CLI: createTempCredentials(submissionID)
  -> BE returns: {accessKeyId, secretAccessKey, sessionToken}
CLI: createBatch(submissionID, "data file", ["data1.csv", "data2.csv"])
  -> BE generates file_id (DRS ID) per file, returns {batchID, files: [{fileName, fileID}, ...]}
CLI: Uploads files directly to S3 using temp credentials
CLI: updateBatch(batchID, [{fileName, succeeded: true}, ...], uploading: true)  // heartbeat
CLI: updateBatch(batchID, [{fileName, succeeded: true}, ...])  // final update
```

### CLI Heartbeat (UploadingMonitor)

- CLI sends `updateBatch(batchID, files, uploading: true)` periodically during upload
- Backend stores batch in an in-memory pool with timestamp
- Scheduler checks every 5 minutes; batches older than 15 minutes without heartbeat are marked `Failed`
- Pool persisted to `logs/uploading_batch_pool.json`

